WEBVTT

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:14.700
Lots of snow today.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:18.580
He's here, sir.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.500
So you're <i>the</i>  Golgo 13, huh?

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:32.300
Would you care for a drink?

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:33.760
State your business.

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:38.470
Stop!

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:42.560
Do it slowly.

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:54.070
This is the man I need you to stamp out for good.

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:56.740
His name is Hewitt.

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:59.410
He's the No. 2 of the syndicate.

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:05.580
He's currently in the process of succeeding the prior boss, Wilson, who died in an auto accident.

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:11.170
But I had doubts about that "accident."

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:16.880
I've known Wilson for a long time and he's not a man who would die in such a careless way.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:21.260
Why was that the only day he drove himself?

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:23.770
Why did those brakes fail?

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:29.400
So I investigated, such as a man like me is prone to do.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:34.820
I didn't find any hard evidence, but all signs still point to Hewitt.

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:37.450
So I came to my verdict:

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:40.450
Guilty!

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:47.000
Before he died, Wilson built up a considerable sum of gold bullions at a downtown bank.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:53.460
In order for Hewitt to accomplish his bloodless coup of the syndicate, he will need to spread cash around.

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:58.970
Which means he needs to get his hands on those bullions.

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:03.010
He has two weeks until the syndicate heads come together for the crowning ceremony.

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:09.020
He needs to be eliminated before that date.

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:15.530
But because he fears an attack from the faction of
syndicate heads who don't recognize his successorship

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:19.490
he never takes even one step out of his windowless room.

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:22.370
But if he does come out

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:30.500
it would be first thing in the morning of the day of the ceremony when he comes to open the bank vault.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:37.010
Your chance to shoot him would be when he gets out of his car and heads for the entrance, however...

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:41.260
...it would be damn near impossible to do it.

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:51.940
I walk unsteadily on paths to nowhere

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:56.070
wondering what I should do right now.

00:02:57.570 --> 00:03:02.530
I play the song you like on the car stereo

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:07.080
with the volume up and my feelings crystallized

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:12.710
driving on streets with no crossroads or signals

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:18.130
with a speed that will catch up with you.

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:22.590
So faraway - let's run!

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:28.890
And let's not bother with the breaks - full throttle.

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:33.190
Oh someday - one of these days

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:38.280
You'll be at my place where nobody can find you.

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:44.370
Whenever you suffer a breakdown one can't see

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:49.950
depend on me for your repairs.

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:54.330
So faraway - let's run!

00:03:54.540 --> 00:04:00.550
We'll reset and start again - even at our limit.

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:04.840
Oh someday - one of these days

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:10.890
If I'm with you we'll find our dream.

00:04:16.270 --> 00:04:21.190
The Best Day of Ash's Life

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:31.750
This time... this time I'll create my brilliant masterpiece...

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.540
Oww...

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:38.040
Morning, Ash!

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:43.970
I see it's never too early to go dumpster diving.

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:46.010
We'll help you out.

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:47.010
Here!

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:49.600
Ow! S-Stop that, you morons!

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:51.060
You punks!

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:53.560
Hey, Mr. Garbage Picker!

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:54.810
Fucking kids!

00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:58.560
Dammit...

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:02.740
What the hell do you take Ash the Prodigy for anyway?

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:06.700
You'll see...

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:13.410
Once I complete my brilliant masterpiece, you all will want a piece of my genius!

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:34.730
You're too goddamn loud, Ash!

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:37.730
Give it a rest ferchrissakes, you dumbfuck!

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:39.690
Hey!

00:05:40.110 --> 00:05:41.730
You're his landlord, right?!

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:43.190
Fucking say something to him!

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:02.210
Gah! What the shit is this?

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:06.260
I didn't rent out this place so you can use it as a goddamn trash heap!

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:09.260
Hey, Mr. Horisky! How are you?

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:13.010
Well I'm sure glad you remember me, Ash.

00:06:13.010 --> 00:06:16.230
So have you decided on paying your back rent?

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:20.520
I did promise to pay you once I sell my artwork, didn't I?

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:22.320
Artwork you say?

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:24.780
Who in God's name would ever buy this junk?

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:32.870
Since you're the only mope squatting in this building, I'm forced to walk so many blocks to collect the rent.

00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:35.910
Why don't you take your garbage and unass yourself from this place?

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:37.620
Wh... What didja just say?!

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:40.830
Are you calling my creations garbage?!

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:43.130
If it's not garbage, then what are they?

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:49.130
I met with an art dealer named Gabriel during Danny's cocktail party!

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:53.180
He said I had talent and to bring over the best one I have!

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:54.640
Hmph!

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:57.520
It was probably just some drug party!

00:06:57.520 --> 00:06:59.440
Huh? What makes you...?

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:00.690
Was it?

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:01.650
Shut the hell up!

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:05.690
Anyway, pay the damn rent!

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:07.990
If you aren't gonna pay, then clear out!

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:08.950
Shuddup!

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:18.450
God, what a shitbird.

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:21.460
If he'd just up and scram, I can finally take this apartment building and...

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:24.170
I'll throw you out myself, goddammit!

00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:28.710
Huh.

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:32.720
One day you'll be bragging about how <i>the</i>  Ash once lived here.

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:36.680
Until then, quit your whining... huh?

00:07:44.060 --> 00:07:46.190
Who's that guy?

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:57.700
What the Christ is that, some fancy-ass vacuum cleaner?

00:07:57.700 --> 00:08:01.080
You got no sense of culture? How the hell is this a vacuum?

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:02.290
This is art, my friend.

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:04.710
Art?

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:08.210
It represents the chaos of decadence.

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:11.800
That fucking went right over my head!

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:15.720
Well, it <i>is</i>  avant-garde.

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:20.470
Once this is done, I'm taking it to Gabriel.

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:25.480
Oh, have you caught sight of this weird Asian dude about 2-3 days ago?

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:30.530
Come on, it'd be easier spotting someone who ain't weird whenever I'm with you!

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:36.490
Well, from what I saw, I'd say he looks Japanese.

00:08:36.490 --> 00:08:39.540
Ohh! That's great 'cause I know a lot about Japan!

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:45.000
A friend of a friend once took a train to Akihabara after returning from the Beijing Olympics!

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:49.050
Get out! He couldn't have gotten there by train!

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:51.510
Akihabara is the capital of Vietnam!

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:53.090
Oh really?

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:56.220
Fine, fuck it all then!

00:08:56.220 --> 00:08:59.560
It's ain't like we're ever gonna go there anyway!

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:00.390
What didja say?

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:03.100
We're stuck here forever.

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:07.440
We ain't gonna be leaving this here place anytime soon.

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:08.860
Oh, I will.

00:09:08.860 --> 00:09:09.400
Huh?

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:14.650
Ash the Prodigy is not gonna be buried here, not if he can help it.

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:18.990
Once I have the money, I'll be saying "sayonara" to this town!

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:34.720
That dumbass, thinks he has a dream or some shit.

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:35.800
Huh?

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:44.850
So that's the Japanese Ash was talking about.

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:47.060
He'll make an easy mark.

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:55.530
Give up some beer money if you don't wanna get hurt!

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:17.470
He must be a damn black belt!

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:54.630
Damn you Gabriel! What do you mean you were too drunk to remember?

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:57.050
Christ! I looked like a total assclown!

00:11:06.310 --> 00:11:07.390
F-Fuck!

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:12.900
Hey, asshole!

00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:15.520
Don't be throwing your garbage, you'll hurt someone!

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:17.570
It <i>ain't</i>  garbage!

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:26.040
God <i>dammit!</i>

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:29.080
Why doesn't anyone get my genius?

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:32.080
Is everybody I come across some kind of lowlife?

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:33.540
Recognize me, dammit!

00:11:35.590 --> 00:11:37.050
Screw off!

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:43.050
I don't got your money! So beat it, Horisky!

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:49.560
Dammit, does he ever give up?

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:54.360
Keep coming all you want, it won't... huh?

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:56.070
Y... You're...

00:12:10.910 --> 00:12:12.370
Ash, right?

00:12:12.370 --> 00:12:13.870
Uh, yeah.

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:15.920
Ahh, hey!

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:17.130
Hey, hold on!

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:19.170
What's your deal?!

00:12:20.420 --> 00:12:23.510
A-Are you... some kind of debt collector?

00:12:23.510 --> 00:12:25.550
I don't got the money!

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:27.760
Threatening me won't change that!

00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:31.810
Hey! Say something!

00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:35.400
What are these?

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:36.270
Huh?

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:39.570
T-They aren't garbage!

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:40.570
How much?

00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:43.070
I'm telling you, they aren't garbage...!

00:12:43.070 --> 00:12:45.780
Huh? What did you just say?

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:47.780
How much are they?

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:51.080
Uhh... um, t-t-ten...

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:53.790
No-no-no! They're $20,000! Yeah, $20,000!

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:54.830
Sold.

00:12:54.830 --> 00:12:56.170
Huh?

00:12:58.460 --> 00:13:00.170
You're... saying you'll buy them?

00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:02.170
That's right.

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:07.680
You got good tastes, pal!

00:13:14.180 --> 00:13:16.600
Ash! Ash!

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:18.190
You in there, Ash?!

00:13:18.860 --> 00:13:19.690
I'm coming in!

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:22.190
Hah?

00:13:24.740 --> 00:13:27.070
W-W-What happened?

00:13:27.070 --> 00:13:28.660
Yo, Horisky!

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:29.200
Huh?

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:30.240
Lobo!

00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:34.370
Where's Ash? Where did he run off to?

00:13:34.370 --> 00:13:36.870
Oh, Ash made wings to Florida.

00:13:36.870 --> 00:13:37.880
Florida?

00:13:38.540 --> 00:13:41.170
He told me to give this to you.

00:13:41.170 --> 00:13:41.590
Huh?

00:13:42.090 --> 00:13:44.630
It's the back rent he owes you.

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:49.390
Where the hell did he get this?

00:13:49.390 --> 00:13:51.350
What happened to all his junk?

00:13:51.350 --> 00:13:54.060
He sold off all of them just like that.

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:58.190
I also got to share in what he had left.

00:13:59.150 --> 00:14:00.360
Say that again?

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:03.860
That guy's a real prodigy, I tell you!

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:06.360
Prodigy?

00:14:26.470 --> 00:14:33.010
<i>Your chance to shoot him would be when he gets out of his car and heads for the entrance, however...</i>

00:14:33.010 --> 00:14:35.970
<i>...it would be damn near impossible to do it.</i>

00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:38.020
Why's that?

00:14:39.190 --> 00:14:43.860
That bank is walled off by the surrounding
apartments that are closely packed together.

00:14:43.860 --> 00:14:46.490
You can't shoot from the outside.

00:14:47.110 --> 00:14:49.910
If even if you try to shoot from one of those buildings

00:14:49.910 --> 00:14:54.120
the army of guards he'll have on that day will be checking things out thoroughly.

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:56.830
Meaning nobody can get near him.

00:14:58.410 --> 00:15:00.040
What I do know is

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:06.510
you're the only person in the world who can pull this off despite those conditions.

00:15:08.010 --> 00:15:10.510
Please, Golgo 13.

00:15:11.050 --> 00:15:15.760
See to it that the rat scurrying behind
those walls receives his death penalty.

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:29.190
I don't believe for a damn second that anyone would buy all that junk.

00:15:29.190 --> 00:15:32.110
I'd like to see what such a mook looks like.

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:39.160
Torisky, right?

00:15:39.160 --> 00:15:40.580
Wha...

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:43.170
What the hell do you want?

00:15:44.210 --> 00:15:46.170
I have a favor to ask.

00:15:47.210 --> 00:15:48.380
A favor?

00:15:51.430 --> 00:15:54.050
So you're sure my security is tight?

00:15:54.550 --> 00:15:56.510
Of course, sir.

00:15:56.510 --> 00:16:00.020
We've deployed the appropriate number of men to the bank.

00:16:00.020 --> 00:16:02.600
Not even a kitten can get anywhere close.

00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:08.570
We've even assembled young men willing to take a bullet for you around the entrance.

00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:12.320
But what if they decide to shoot me from the outside?

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:14.070
No need to worry.

00:16:14.870 --> 00:16:19.120
The street in front of the bank is narrow and it's completely walled in.

00:16:20.330 --> 00:16:23.580
We've checked out everybody living in those apartments.

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:27.250
It's just thugs, call-girls, their pimps...

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:29.090
...basically just a bunch of lowlifes.

00:16:29.760 --> 00:16:32.590
None of them are going to pose any threat to you, boss.

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:35.640
Well, I hope so.

00:16:37.470 --> 00:16:41.100
Did you stop to think that a pro might be among those lowlifes?

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:43.140
Don't worry.

00:16:43.140 --> 00:16:47.060
If anyone tries to point a gun from one of those buildings

00:16:47.060 --> 00:16:49.610
they'll be instantly swiss-cheesed by our machine guns.

00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:52.610
Maybe there's some suicidal jamoke out there.

00:16:52.610 --> 00:16:57.120
But a pro that keeps an escape route in
mind wouldn't do something so stupid.

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:01.910
I get my meals from this street, so I guarantee everything.

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:05.670
Anyway...

00:17:06.210 --> 00:17:08.670
Everything will work out if we take care of this.

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:11.840
Nobody will dare oppose me after this.

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:16.640
After this, I will be the syndicate's No. 1, in name and spirit.

00:17:17.140 --> 00:17:18.680
That's right.

00:17:19.010 --> 00:17:21.970
You already have the syndicate in the palm of your hand...

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:23.640
...boss.

00:17:34.950 --> 00:17:36.990
All right, you may go!

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:33.500
Sorry to keep you.

00:18:58.360 --> 00:19:00.160
W-What is this?

00:19:19.220 --> 00:19:21.010
B... Boss!

00:19:21.010 --> 00:19:21.720
Huh?

00:19:26.310 --> 00:19:27.310
Over there!

00:19:27.310 --> 00:19:28.890
The building behind it!

00:19:33.770 --> 00:19:34.770
What the...?

00:19:43.990 --> 00:19:45.830
Boss! Boss!

00:19:45.530 --> 00:19:47.990
Hey, search behind it!

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:47.990
Hang in there, boss!

00:19:50.250 --> 00:19:51.370
Jesus.

00:19:51.370 --> 00:19:53.540
Who the hell was that guy?

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:04.180
Not a minute after Ash left, I get a buyer for that apartment building!

00:20:04.180 --> 00:20:06.260
God, what luck!

00:20:06.260 --> 00:20:09.770
But boy was I shocked when that Asian fella said he'd pay cash!

00:20:09.770 --> 00:20:14.770
The way he looks freaks me out, but he must be <i>the</i>  God of Fortune!

00:20:20.530 --> 00:20:22.780
So he really did it!

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:26.830
That Golgo 13 sure lives up to his fame.

00:20:27.280 --> 00:20:31.330
Still, to bring down an entire apartment
building while configuring the ballistics...

00:20:31.330 --> 00:20:34.290
He comes up with some incredible ideas.

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:37.340
It was a good idea...

00:20:37.340 --> 00:20:43.300
...but when that apartment building imploded nobody can see though the dust it created.

00:20:43.300 --> 00:20:47.350
During that implosion, it would have taken him a moment's time to aim.

00:20:47.350 --> 00:20:50.810
And add to that the range he had to shoot from...

00:20:50.810 --> 00:20:55.560
Even if he did come up with a good idea, that man...

00:20:56.150 --> 00:21:00.570
Only a Golgo 13 could ever pull off a stunt like that.

00:21:00.570 --> 00:21:02.570
No doubt about it.

00:21:04.150 --> 00:21:06.620
He's a real miracle man.

00:21:07.620 --> 00:21:11.580
So the rumors are true, you are the world's top sniper.

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:14.000
Golgo 13.

00:21:34.890 --> 00:21:36.900
I'm telling you girls.

00:21:36.900 --> 00:21:42.860
This guy who's obviously loaded comes asking me to sell him my art, not even knowing how much they're worth.

00:21:43.740 --> 00:21:47.110
But that guy bought all of them right?

00:21:47.610 --> 00:21:48.530
Yeah...

00:21:48.530 --> 00:21:53.160
He begged me to sell him everything, what can I do?

00:21:53.160 --> 00:21:55.620
Wow, that's so amazing!

00:21:57.080 --> 00:22:00.670
Well, he's got pretty good tastes for a Japanese.

00:22:00.670 --> 00:22:02.840
Plus he's generous with the dough.

00:22:02.840 --> 00:22:05.970
I think I might just take a trip to the Orient.

00:22:05.970 --> 00:22:08.930
Once I get bored here, maybe I'll do Japan.

00:22:08.930 --> 00:22:10.680
Oh no!

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:10.680
Don't go!

00:22:10.680 --> 00:22:12.140
Take me with you!

00:22:12.140 --> 00:22:15.140
Huh? Fine, you can all tag along.

00:22:15.140 --> 00:22:16.770
Whee! How wonderful!

00:22:16.770 --> 00:22:18.020
Really?

00:22:18.020 --> 00:22:21.060
Really. But let's hold that thought.

00:22:22.440 --> 00:22:26.280
For now, let's raise a glass to the greatest day of my life.

00:22:43.920 --> 00:22:47.220
I  was worried with no one to talk to.

00:22:47.220 --> 00:22:50.260
I was brooding and standing still

00:22:50.260 --> 00:22:52.430
without moving a muscle.

00:22:53.100 --> 00:22:55.600
I wonder when that was?

00:22:56.100 --> 00:22:57.310
I'm sure

00:22:57.310 --> 00:23:00.480
you agonized over how

00:23:00.480 --> 00:23:05.730
people will hurt themselves and other people

00:23:06.360 --> 00:23:08.990
and fail to realize it.

00:23:09.360 --> 00:23:10.110
When

00:23:10.110 --> 00:23:13.530
the same days keep repeating themselves

00:23:13.530 --> 00:23:15.790
you never change.

00:23:16.490 --> 00:23:18.040
Since you're here for me

00:23:18.040 --> 00:23:22.330
I will accept the way that I am.

00:23:23.040 --> 00:23:26.590
I will never leave you alone

00:23:26.590 --> 00:23:29.930
I will softly touch your trembling heart.

00:23:30.130 --> 00:23:36.810
I realized that I'm not the only one who's alone.

00:23:36.810 --> 00:23:39.980
We're enveloped in the gentle sun beams.

00:23:39.980 --> 00:23:43.310
The long winter is finally over.

00:23:43.310 --> 00:23:49.950
The parts of us that were lonely will surely get stronger.

00:24:01.710 --> 00:24:05.630
Golgo is facing a sniper names Spartacus.

00:24:05.630 --> 00:24:08.630
It was two millionaires who devised the showdown.

00:24:08.630 --> 00:24:14.050
They fixedly watched the whole spectacle through a monitor.

00:24:14.050 --> 00:24:17.720
The gunshots echo through the silent Colosseum.

00:24:17.720 --> 00:24:20.850
An unforeseen development awaits the two of them.

00:24:20.230 --> 00:24:26.020
The Brutes' Banquet

00:24:20.850 --> 00:24:24.230
Next time on Golgo 13: The Brutes' Banquet.

00:24:24.230 --> 00:24:28.360
Don't stand behind him, if you value your life.
